ary classroom that becomes an open lab","notes":"Check the room schedule before arriving, then use the installed computers when instruction is not occupying the room.","short_summary":"A computer-equipped classroom with a clearly documented open-lab use between scheduled instruction sessions.","evidence_claim":"The official Gould Library tour identifies Room 306 as a library classroom and computer lab that is open when not being used for instruction.","source_url":"https://gouldguides.carleton.edu/c.php?g=147169&p=965873","source_title":"Classrooms and Computer Labs — Library Tour","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2025-05-29","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Available as an open computer lab only when it is not scheduled for a library instruction session.","cost_status":"not_applicable","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"writing-center-420","subject_type":"study_space","entity_name":"Writing Center, Gould Library 420","title":"Bring a Draft to the Writing Center","subtitle":"Fourth-floor space for guided writing work","notes":"Reserve a conference for focused feedback, or try a walk-in while remembering that scheduled writers receive priority.","short_summary":"A dedicated place to develop writing with a peer consultant from brainstorming through final proofreading.","evidence_claim":"A Carleton course resource locates the Writing Center in Room 420 on Gould Library’s fourth floor and documents appointments, walk-ins, and peer help across the writing process.","source_url":"https://cdn.carleton.edu/uploads/sites/64/2020/09/122F20.pdf","source_title":"POSC 122: Politics in America — Course Resources","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Appointments have priority over walk-ins; consult the current Writing Center schedule before visiting Room 420.","cost_s